details:
(a) whether it is a fact that there are weapons and weapon system in Defence kitty worth hundreds of crores of rupees like Harpy missile purchased from Israel, anti sea-eagle missile, anti-radiation missiles and some types of cluster bombs which have either developed some defects, or their parts are no longer available in the market;
(b) if so, the steps taken by Government to make them fit for use;
(c) if not, the reasons therefor; and
(d) what would be the disposal of such weapons and weapon systems?

(a) whether it is fact that State Bank of India (SBI) has restricted the use of ATMs by introducing service charges beyond a certain number of withdrawals;
(b) if so, the details in this regard and the reasons therefor;
(c) whether the decision is against promoting ATM culture and against the interest of customers;
(d) whether the bank proposes to review these measures; and
(e) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the foodstock available before the current spell of drought in the country;
(b) the outflow of foodgrains to each of the drought affected States in the country in recent months; and
(c) the current size of foodstocks left?

(a) whether it is a fact that there is considerable tension and signs of fatigue amongst Central Researve Police Force personnel because of continuous postings and other factors;
(b) whether the signs of stress are leading to tendencies of suicide and murder etc.;
(c) whether it is also a fact that there is no system for redressal of their grievances; and
(d) the steps Government has taken to address this problem?

(a) whether it is a fact that about 100 Air Force pilots have sought voluntary retirement;
(b) if so, the reasons given by these pilots in support of their requests; and
(c) the action Government has taken on their requests and to augment the strength and increase the number of pilots in the Air Force?

(SHRI A.K. ANTONY)
MINISTER OF DEFENCE
(a) to (c): Around 101 pilots of IAF have applied for grant of Premature Retirement during the last one year. The broad reasons furnished by the applicants for grant of Premature Retirement are Supersession, Lack of Career Progression, Medical/compassionate etc. Such applications are considered on a case to case basis in accordance with extant Government policy and service exigencies. Concerted efforts are taken by the Indian Air Force to carry out a proactive publicity campaign to reach the target group across the country, such as 
(i) participation in career fairs and exhibitions to enhance one-to-one interaction; 
(ii) advertisement in print and electronic media including recruitment and career related articles; 
(iii) motivational lectures in schools/colleges; 
(iv) distribution of publicity material to target group; 
(v) visuals/signages at vantage points all over the country at strategic locations. The Short Service Commission for Flying branch has been modified to make men also eligible for induction in this branch. The implementation of the recommendations of VIth Central Pay Commission will also go a long way in attracting youth.

(a) whether the State Bank of India (SBI) has started levying pass book updation charge, fee for depositing cash at branches other than the one where the account is opened, cheque book charge, minimum balance charge etc;
(b) if so, the reasons therefor;
(c) whether the bank is thus depriving the customers of whatever little rates of interest it pays;
(d) whether it is causing hardships to senior citizens and pensioners necessitating them to visit their branch to escape these charges;
(e) whether the SBI proposes to review these unpopular arrangements; and
(f) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether it is a fact that the countries like USA and European Union are trying to scuttle the Kyoto Protocol mechanism with a World Bank type institution to manage climate change funding;
(b) if so, whether Government has voiced its concern at the international platform;
(c) if so, the details in this regard; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the current position in respect of amount of sugarcane arrears mill owners owe to the farmers in Uttar Pradesh;
(b) whether the arrears have declined in the last one year or so;
(c) if so, the reasons therefor;
(d) whether the sugarcane arrears is one deterrent factor which discourages farmers from cultivation of sugarcane;
(e) whether Government proposes to intervene with a view to compel mill owners to clear the arrears within a time bound framework; and
(f) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether it is a fact that there is a stockpile of carpets with carpet manufacturers in Bhadohi near Varanasi;
(b) whether it is also a fact that low demand is due to absence of western buyers, absence of clear tax regime, non availability of special incentives, bank credit etc.; and
(c) the steps taken by Government to help the industry on these counts?

(a) what were the important issues that were taken up during G20 Pittsburgh Summit which concluded recently;
(b) whether Global Crisis Management was one of the items discusses there;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether it is also a fact that Pittsburgh marked the emergence of G-20 as the premium forum for international Economic co-operation replacing G-7; and
(e) whether Government is satisfied with the outcome?

(a) the names of the rivers which have been declared dead due to industrial and man made activities resulting in extreme pollution as in the case of Yamuna in Delhi;
(b) what are the reasons that Government has not so far learnt any lesson to revive Yamuna and other such rivers, from the rivers abroad like Hudson in New York, Thames in London, Seine in Paris, Tiber in Rome, Nile in Cairo and Cheonggyecheon stream in Seoul; and
(c) whether any such plans are likely to start in near future for these rivers including Yamuna?

(a) the total annual sale of khadi in the country in the last three years, year-wise;
(b) the quantum of export in the last three years, year-wise;
(c) the quantum of subsidy given on khadi during the same period, year-wise; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure that the amount of subsidy reaches the targeted individuals and organizations?

(a) whether it is a fact that over two-thirds of the agricultural land is still dependant on rains;
(b) whether it is also a fact that China has only one-third of its agricultural land unirrigated;
(c) whether it is also a fact that developed countries depend very little on rains; and
(d) if so, the action Government has taken to create infrastructural projects in the recent past 
to relieve agriculture of its dependence on rains?

(a) whether it is a fact that there is a pulse war among phone service providers;
(b) whether Government has made any assessment on this front for the years to come;
(c) the steps MTNL has taken to compete in this war of rates;
(d) whether it proposes to reduce the fixed line tariff, increase the number of free calls and reduce the rate of calls to promote the ever increasing desertation of fixed line phones; and 
(e) it not, the reasons therefor?

(a) what are the annual earnings from the Gurgaon railway station in Haryana;
(b) whether it is a fact that about 20,000 passengers use railway station everyday which contributes more than Rs.60 crores every year; and 
(c) if so, what are the reasons that basic amenities have not been provided at this station including the ones promised years back for e.g. provision for coolies, installation of camera facilities, adequate halt time and state of the art restaurant etc.?

(a) what is the quantity of wheat procured by FCI in Punjab and Haryana this summer;
(b) whether it is a fact that FCI has started moving out fresh stocks of wheat to consuming States ignoring `first in, first out` norm;
(c) if so, what are the reasons therefor; and
(d) what is the quantity of old stocks of wheat still lying with FCI?

(a) whether it is a fact that India and Pakistan have begun bilateral talks on Kishanganga project through the joint water commission;
(b) whether it is a fact that differences continue among Pakistan officials over India`s position on the project; and
(c) whether there is any possibility of these differences being resolved in the near future?

(a) whether it is a fact that a new study of major river systems of the world has revealed that Ganga is rapidly loosing its water;
(b) if so, the reasons for this phenomenon, according to study;
(c) whether the feasibility of taking any short-term measures has been examined; and
(d) if so, with what results?

(a) whether it is a fact that a CSIR laboratory has developed a Thin Film Composite (TFC) reverse osmosis (RO) high flux membrane for recovering process water for industrial use from domestic sewage through tertiary treatment; 
(b) whether the technique has been used on a mass scale for treatment of water;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the target for tax collection for the financial year 2008-09;
(b) whether it is a fact that these tax collections have fallen short of the target; and
(c) if so, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether it is a fact that, form 49(O) were not provided at a large number of polling booths in the recent general elections for the benefit of voters wanting to express their disapproval of the candidates contesting the elections, as per the media reports published in a section of the press;
(b) if so, the estimated number of booths in the country which were not having these forms; and
(c) the reasons therefore?

(a) whether it is a fact that high alert has been sounded in the Corbett National Park following a major fire in the periphery of Uttarakhand Park in April this year;
(b) if so, the current status of fire; and 
(c) the steps taken to prevent recurrence of such fire incidents?

(a) the number of forests that caught fire this summer and the number of incidents of fire reported, giving the details, State-wise;
(b) whether the fire incidents were successfully controlled in all cases;
(c) the details of the damage caused by these fire incidents; and
(d) the long term arrangements made to control or prevent such incidents?

(a) the assessment made so far about the Polymetallic Nodules Projects;
(b) the amount spent on the project, so far;
(c) whether the achievements have been commensurate with the expenditure incurred on the project; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor ?

(a) whether it is a fact that a technology has been developed by a CSIR laboratory for removal of arsenic/ iron from ground water by using ceramic membranes and another technology comprising of microbial cum adsorbent route;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether the technology has been used in areas having ground water affected with arsenic and leading to a number of health problems; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor ?

(a) whether it is a fact that Government is considering a proposal to withdraw CRPF from Kashmir and hand over the security operations to local police;
(b) if so, the reasons therefor; and 
(c) whether Government has proposed to review the capability of local police before handing over the operations to them?

(a) whether Government has assessed the working of employment exchanges against the present day complex nature of the job market;
(b) if so, with what results thereto;
(c) whether Government is considering any proposal to reorient, modernize or abolish the system; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor ?

(a) whether Government is considering a proposal to take steps under WTO against protectionist measures being taken by developed countries in a range of sectors including steel;
(b) whether it is a fact that world over protectionism has taken new forms that needs to be addressed; and
(c) the details of steps being considered or taken in this regard?

(a) whether it is a fact that export scene is likely to remain grim this year too;
(b) if so, what are the reasons coming in the way of recovery of exports; and
(c) the steps being contemplated to address the problem?

(a) the quantum of withdrawals by States of the Northern and Southern regions from the 
National Grid, during the last four months;
(b) whether it is a fact that there have been overdrawals from the grid during that period; 
and
(c) the steps Government has taken to avert collapse of the grid?

(a) Whether it is a fact that Pune based National Film Archives of India sold around 25,000 film reels as waste, last year;
(b) Whether it is also a fact that many of those reels related to old and rare titles of which copies may not be available anywhere; and 
(c) If so, the action Government has taken in this matter?

(a) whether Government’s attention has been drawn to recent media reports about the spurious milk being manufactured at a large scale in North India;
(b) whether it is a fact that State owned milk producers like Mother Dairy and
DMS etc. also procure milk from these vendors;
(c) if so, the details of the precautions these producers take or have taken to ensure that the quality of milk produced by them is genuine; and
(d) the action Government has taken against the spurious milk producers?

(a) when was the concept of rain water harvesting introduced in the country;
(b) whether any scientific advancements have been introduced in the concept since then;
(c) whether Government has made any assessments about the gains from this concept;
(d) if so, the details in this regard;
(e) whether any scientific advancement are proposed to be added to the concept and 
(f) if so, the details in this regard?

(a) whether it is a fact that Kosi river is now being watched through satellite;
(b) if so, the names of the agencies that are doing the job;
(c) whether any data has come up suggesting risky flow of water in the months ahead and/or any embankments still needing repairs; and
(d) if so, the action contemplated in the matter?

(a) whether Government has issued a notification listing documents that are necessary for obtaining a driving licence;
(b) if so, the details of documents required to be furnished for obtaining a driving licence;
(c) whether the documents like voter ID cards have not been considered as sufficient ID proof;
(d) if so, the reasons therefor;
(e) whether the PAN card is must for applying for a driving licence
(f) if so, the reasons therefor; and 
(g) whether Government proposes to review the notification and if not, the reasons therefor?

THE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE
MINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS 
(SHRI MAHADEO SINGH KHANDELA)
(a)&(b) Government has prescribed certain documents out of which anyone could be submitted by the applicant as proof of deemed citizen or citizen by birth. These documents are listed below:-
(i) Proof of birth in India from municipality or Registrar of Births and Deaths; 
(ii) School leaving certificate/Secondary School certificate showing nationality/place of birth; 
(iii) Passport showing place of birth/citizenship/nationality; 
(iv) Certificate of Nationality/citizenship issued by District Magistrate or any other Administrative officer; 
(v) Residency Permit/domicile certificate issued by the State Government; 
(vi) Grant of patta/lease of property by the Central/State Government; 
(vii)Refugee Registration Card pertaining to the period 1947-1950; 
(viii) Certificate of SC/ST/OBC.
(c)&(d) Voter ID has not been included in the list. Since the requirement of proof of citizenship has been made to prevent illegal migrants from obtaining a statutory document like driving licence, the list would be further expanded on the advice of Ministry of Home Affairs. 
(e)&(f) PAN Card is not required for applying for driving licence. 
(g) Review of rules and notifications issued there under is a continuous process.

(a) whether it is a fact that admission to some courses in
 Universities e.g. Delhi University is conducted on the basis
 of the Combined Entrance Test;
(b) if so , the details of the courses admission to which
is so conducted;
(c) whether it is also a fact that this negates the
 importance of the performance in the qualifying examination;
 and
(d) if so, what is the justification of the entrance test?

(a) whether it is a fact that pension of pay scales of S-28, S-29 and S-30 is less than what the Pay Commission had recommended;
(b) whether the pre-revised pay scales of S-24 to S-27 were upgraded from pay band 3 to 4 and S-31 and S-32 were given a separate higher pay scale but S-28, S-29 and S-30 not only did not get any proportionate increase but actually got downgraded from Rs. 39200—67000 to Rs. 37400—67000;
(c) if so, the reasons therefor; and
(d) the steps proposed to undo the harm to the affected categories?

(a) whether it is a fact that a number of people serving on regulatory boards of the Ministry are also directors of companies whose projects the boards, they are serving on, have appraised;
(b) if so, the details in this regard; and
(c) what action Government has contemplated against them?

(a) whether Government has taken stock of the projects which are either unfinished or yet to take off for the Commonwealth Games and the time now left;
(b) if so, the details of these projects and steps taken to complete them timely; 
(c) whether it is a fact that in totality Delhi still presents a bad picture so far as hygiene, road conditions and traffic jams are concerned; and
(d) the steps being taken to address all these problems?

(a) whether Government has made any assessment of the waste generated by urban India, annually;
(b) whether it is a fact that there is no systematic disposal of urban waste as pointed out by a CAG Audit Report recently;
(c) whether Government is considering steps towards scientific management of waste in urban areas of the country; and 
(d) if so, the details in this regard?

(a) the size of current stock of cotton available in the country in relation to the corresponding stock last year;
(b) the current size of requirements;
(c) whether it is a fact that the Cotton Corporation of India is hoarding the stock of cotton;
(d) if so, the reasons therefor;
(e) whether Government is considering a proposal to regulate the activities of the Corporation; and
(f) if so, the details in this regard?

(a) whether it is a fact that Government has increased the Minimum Support Price 
(MSP) for the cotton this year;
(b) if so, the details in this regard and the quantum of cotton procured so far this year;
(c) whether it is also a fact that the steep increase in MSP did not take into account the global downturn, thus creating perpetual problems for the textile industry and the Cotton Corporation of India (CCI) as the prices are not likely to firm up soon; and
(d) how does Government proposes to resolve this problem?

(a) whether it is a fact that a plan for coastal security was initiated in 2005;
(b) if so, the details thereof including that of infrastructure sought to be provided and amount allocated for the plan;
(c) what are the details of the amount released so far, year-wise and the infrastructure created till date;
(d) whether it is also a fact that progress continues to be tardy under the plan thus neglecting coastal security of the country; and
(e) the steps contemplated for speedy implementation of the plan?

(a) the current status of environmental pollution in the Yamuna river;
(b) whether it is a fact that Yamuna river got much dirtier recently when water plants had to be closed due to non-availability of power resulting in considerable increase of ammonia in its water;
(c) whether any action has been taken against power supply companies in this regard; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government has enquired into Guwahati Blasts that took place on the new year`s day this year;
(b) if so, what are the findings;
(c) whether Government has taken up the matter with Bangladesh Government; and
(d) if so, the results thereof?

(a) whether it is a fact that the science behind Narco-Analysis is outdated, its practicality unproven, ethics dubious and findings not maintainable in courts;
(b) whether it is also a fact that the method of conducting the test is far from satisfactory and is liable to have side effects that ultimately may prove dangerous, if not fatal; and
(c) if so, the reasons that this is not discontinued in the country when such tests are not conducted else where in any lab of the world?

(a) whether it is a fact that imports from China have exceeded Rs.40,000 crores during 2008- 09;
(b) if so, whether Government is contemplating making out a case of dumping and considering steps against dumping; and
(c) if so, the details in this regard?

(a) whether it is a fact that a ship ‘SS Oceanic’ carrying 250 tonnes of asbestos, a toxic material, was headed for Alang in Saurashtra coast;
(b) whether it is a fact that Alang Ship Breaking Yard has earned infamy because of its poor handling of toxic waste from dismantled ships; and 
(c) if so, the steps Government has taken on both the counts?

(a) the total area covered in the country by agriculture;
(b) whether there has been any decline in the area covered under agriculture in the last three 
years, year-wise;
(c) whether Government has considered increasing the area under agriculture and raising more 
crops than at present keeping in view of the size of population and environmental dangers ahead; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether India contributes to the budget in respect of the International Rice Research Institute, in Philippine;
(b) if so, the details of the country`s contribution to the institute for the last three years, year-wise;
(c) whether it is a fact that the Institute is facing cuts in its budget at a time when the damage to rice crops, food scarcity and high prices threaten the overall food security; and
(d) whether Government proposes to provide additional help to the Institute?

(a) whether it is a fact that Supreme Court has imposed an interim stay on the increase in the fines for violation of traffic rules, earlier ordered by Delhi High Court;
(b) if so, when was this order given;
(c) when was the copy of the order collected by the Traffic Police and the date when it was implemented;
(d) the total amount collected at enhanced rate after the date of order and before implementation of order; and
(e) what is the mode of disposal of enhanced fines collected after the date of order and before implementation of order?

(a) what is the amount collected by way of taxes from Gujarat in the last 3 years, year-wise;
(b) what was the amount of Central funds provided to the State during that period, year-wise; 
(c) what percentage did the Central funds constitute of the tax collection, year-wise; and
(d) whether the percentage nearly holds good for all the States?

(a) Whether it is fact that chunk of heritage films have been lost forever; 
(b) whether it is also a fact that a majority of films that have vanished without a trace, dating back to 1930s and 1940s;
(c) The reasons for which the Film Board of India did not act in the matter;
(d) Whether Government proposes to enlist public cooperation in retrieving prints of those films, to the extent possible; and
(e) If not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether it is a fact that calls made from Delhi to NCR towns and vice vers are still not treated as local calls and don not materialize without a STD code particularly to places like Palwal, Sonepat, Meerut, Alwar, gurgaon etc.; 
(b) if so, the reasons thereof; 
(c) whether it is a fact that the city code does not enable many land line and mobile phones to access these cities due to poor technology or other reasons;
(d) whether this defeats the concept of NCR; and 
(e) whether Government proposes to address the matter?

(a) whether it is a fact that country`s iron-ore experts have advised on restricting or stopping altogether the export of iron-ore as it is considered worse than selling family silver;
(b) the factors that prevent us from selling it at best prices in the world than dumping it at cheapest prices;
(c) if so, whether Government has taken any decision on export of iron-ore; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether it is a fact that extreme parts of coastal areas of southern India, particularly the sea beaches of Kanyakumari have high levels of natural radiation that emanates from the minerals found on beaches; 
(b) whether it is a fact that a new study has revealed that radiation figures in some places near Kanyakumari are 50 times more than the world average and this could be a cause for cancer; and 
(c) if so, whether Government has taken any steps to address the problem and warn visitors to the area, and if not, the reasons therefore?

(a) whether it is a fact that there is shortage of fertilizers in different parts of
 the country;
(b) if so, the details in this regard;
(c) whether it is also a fact that production of fertilizers in the country has
 gone down following closure of some plants; and
(d) the steps Government has taken to address the problem?

(a) the number of projects currently in progress in Arunachal Pradesh and the total length of roads proposed to be built there; 
(b) whether any time-frame has been fixed for the purpose; and
(c) if so, the details in this regard?

(a) whether it is a fact that different types of crime has registered increase in the National Capital Region (NCR) in the last one year or so;
(b) whether it is also a fact that in the lost 5 months alone 180 cases of snatching took place in Delhi;
(c) whether the number of murders, rapes, robberies, incidents of road rage and fatal accidents involving police personnel and other in Delhi, Noida, Gurgaon, Greater Noida, etc. have considerably increased; and
(d) if so, the reasons therefor and the step taken to curb the crime?

(a) whether it is a fact that a devastating dust storm hit Kanpur city on 14th May, 2008;
(b) whether it is also a fact that a large number of villages in the area were gutted in fire stoked by winds; and
(c) if so, the details of the loss of life and property and extent of relief provided to the victims?

(a) whether Government has recently imposed export duty on rice;
(b) if so, the details in this regard;
(c) whether it is a fact that as a result of imposition of export duty, 
 domestic exporters have been faltering on commitments;
(d) whether some importers have threatened law suits against Indian 
 rice exporters;
(e) if so, whether the country is likely to lose its credibility in 
 the international market; and
(f) if so, the steps being taken in the matter?

(a) whether it is a fact that Government has decided to junk the anti-malarial
 drug chloroquine in favour of a new drug combination;
(b) if so, what are the details in this regard;
(c) whether any clinical trials of the new combination of drugs have been carried out;
 and
(d) if so, the results thereof?

(a) whether it is a fact that a recent study by the Central Ground Water Board (CGWB) had indicated that the ground water in over 200 districts of the country has a high level of flouride and arsenic, posing a big public-health hazard;
(b) whether it is also a fact that among 184 districts across 19 States, Rajasthan is the worst placed with all its 32 districts at risk, while Orissa and Gujarat have 18 districts in the danger list, as revealed in the CGWB website; and 
(c) if so, the steps Government has taken to address the problem?

(a) what are the details of the areas where oil drilling is currently going on;
(b) what is the current estimated potential of oil in these areas;
(c) whether it is a fact that oil drilling in some areas has also been given to private sector;
(d) if so, what are the details in this regard and the estimated potential; and
(e) what would be the total production of oil after all these areas have been exploited vis-à-vis current production?

(a) the number of people currently unemployed as per the records of Employment Exchanges and otherwise; 
(b) whether it is a fact that in the present context Employment Exchanges have ceased to be meaningful places for providing employment as major part of employment is being generated by private sector openly and there is a little of Government placement; and 
(c) whether Government is considering any proposal to make these Employment Exchanges more useful to the community?

(a) whether it is a fact that the Federation of Film Societies of India, established by Late Shri Satyajit Ray and Shrimati Indira Gandhi has been receiving grant-in-aid for about 25 years;
(b) if so, the details of grant given in the last few years;
(c) whether it is also a fact that grant-in-aid has been discontinued recently; if so, what are the reasons for discontinuing the grant; and
(d) if not, what is the amount released in the current financial year, i.e. 2007-08?

(a) whether it is a fact that the Federation of Film Societies of India, an apex organisation of 300 film societies in the country, proposes to celebrate Golden Jubilee year in 2008-09;
(b) if so, whether Government is considering any proposal to release special grant to the Federation;
(c) if so, the details in this regard; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the number of Advanced Jet Trainers (AJTs) Government has received so far recently from abroad;
(b) the total number of AJTs likely to be received from abroad in the near future from various sources;
(c) whether Government is also considering a proposal to start its production in the country; and
(d) if so, the details in this regard?

(a) whether Government has resolved the differences with Russia over the purchase of the aircraft carrier Admiral Gorshkov during the visit of Russian PM Viktor Zubkov to India recently;
(b) if so, the details thereof; and
(c) the other issues that were discussed with the visiting dignitary?

(a) whether it is a fact that LPG dealers in the Northern part of the country have created an artificial shortage of LPG cylinders;
(b) if so, the steps Government has taken against the erring dealers;
(c) whether Government is considering any proposal to start the sale of LPG cylinders through petrol pumps in a convenient packing; and 
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government’s attention has been drawn to reports of China joining the Pakistan-Iran Gas Pipeline Project in the event of India not joining the project; 
(b) whether it is a fact that in the event of India not joining the project, the pipeline is likely to pass through Gilgit, a strategic place in the PoK;
(c) whether Government is aware that the road connecting Pakistan and China and passing through that area is proposed to be widened for the purpose; 
(d) if so, whether Government has considered this move; and 
(e) if so, with what results?

(a) whether it is a fact that drugs banned in a number of countries continues to be on sale in the country;
(b) if so, what are the reasons therefor;
(c) whether it is also a fact that the list of banned drugs includes medicines like Nimesulide, banned in over 170 countries, and at least 11 drugs, used for common cures continue to be sold freely in the country; 
(d) whether it is a fact that this poor State of affairs is due to absence of poor monitoring mechanism; and
(e) if so, the steps Government have taken in this regard?

(a) whether it is a fact that the High Court of Delhi has directed the Central Government as well as Government of Delhi to set up the Grievance Redressal Committee in each of their hospitals to help improve facilities for patients within a given time-frame;
(b) if so, what are the details in this regard;
(c) whether these Committees will also take up complaints from patients and visitors or merely attend to staff related problems; and
(d) the action Government has taken so far for setting up these Committees?

(a) the estimated production of cotton this season;
(b) the estimated requirement of cotton in the country, particularly in the handloom sector;
(c) the estimates of world-wide production and whether there is any shortfall; and
(d) the steps being taken to meet the deficit, if any, in the ensuing season?

(a) whether it is a fact that a directory is periodically brought out showing names of officers of the rank of Joint Secretary and above posted in various Ministries and departments of Government;
(b) whether it is also a fact that the directory does not contain State-wise details of officers drawn from the respective States;
(c) if so, whether Government proposes to incorporate these details; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Indian Meteorological Department has studied the extreme changes reflected in the weather patterns in the northern and other parts of the country this year;
(b) whether any observations have been made on the causes of extreme weather or the trends to come; and
(c) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether it is a fact that booming economy has failed to check unemployment in the country; 
